// check-feme-capability-manifest.py (roadmap WS3(b)) must name which
// specific row of a capability-manifest table drifted from its generator,
// not just report "something changed", and must also report a manifest
// that still matches as "unchanged" without raising a false alarm.
//
// Inputs/check-feme-capability-manifest/feme stands in for the real
// feme/ subtree: its fake vk_gen_feature_inventory.py/
// vk_gen_extension_inventory.py always emit a fixed two-row table
// regardless of their (ignored) vk.xml/version/advertised-file arguments,
// so this test exercises check-feme-capability-manifest.py's own diff
// logic, not the real generators or a real vk.xml. The fixture's
// Vulkan14FeatureInventory.md table matches the fake feature generator's
// output exactly (the "unchanged" path); its VulkanExtensionInventory.md
// table deliberately differs in one row from the fake extension
// generator's output (the "drifted" path), so one run of the script
// covers both outcomes.
//
// RUN: not %python %S/../../utils/check-feme-capability-manifest.py \
// RUN:   --vk-xml %S/Inputs/check-feme-capability-manifest/fake-vk.xml \
// RUN:   --feme-source-dir \
// RUN:     %S/Inputs/check-feme-capability-manifest/feme \
// RUN:   --python %python > %t.out 2>&1
// RUN: FileCheck %s < %t.out
//
// CHECK: Vulkan14FeatureInventory: unchanged
// CHECK: VulkanExtensionInventory: drifted
// CHECK-NEXT: ---
// CHECK-NEXT: +++
// CHECK: -| `VK_FAKE_extension_two` | Not implemented |  |
// CHECK: +| `VK_FAKE_extension_two` | Advertised |  |
